@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Explicitly add or remove active stories
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "SprintBoardPage, SprintsPage, BacklogPage\nor a work page; SprintScopeDialog / SprintScopeForm" as page
  participant "ISprintService / SprintService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "SprintsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "ChangeSprintScopeCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "Sprint" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
group Open the dialog (read on open)
  actor -> page : Change scope or Add stories (sprintId), Backlog Add to sprint (sprintId, addStoryId),\nor Remove (sprintId, removeStoryId, removeStorySummary); every opener passes offerSprintsLink,\nfalse only from the Sprints tab
  page -> client : sprintPlanResource(GetSprintPlanQuery): title, dates, version;\nadd mode also reads the eligible candidates (eligibleOnly true, page 1), and with addStoryId one eligible\nread with storyId: the story starts chosen only if that read returns it; otherwise nothing is chosen
  client --> page : Add and Return to backlog disabled until the sprint resolves (loading); a failed read shows Try again\n(reload) and Cancel, with the reference ID only after a 500 (load-failed); a 404 emits notFound: the dialog\ncloses with Outdated and the opening page rereads
end
actor -> page : Choose stories across search and pages (eligible only), or confirm Remove\nfor one unfinished story, in SprintScopeDialog
page -> client : Build typed ChangeSprintScopeCommand with the version from the sprint resource
client -> access : PUT /api/workspaces/{id}/sprints/{sprintId}/scope
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once; sign in with the sprint board as return route
else Authenticated (profile P: every active role changes sprint scope)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send ChangeSprintScopeCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : At least one story; distinct IDs; no story both added and removed
  alt Empty or malformed change
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read or changed
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Keep the selection so it can be corrected; the failed alert shows the server's reason without\nTry again or reference ID; Add (or Return to backlog) is still offered, so focus stays on it
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle ChangeSprintScopeCommand
    handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync (workspace lock); LoadScopeChangeAsync:\nSprint with status, version and memberships; its BoardState; named stories with status and open membership
    db --> handler : Current scope, unchanged initial scope, eligibility
    alt Sprint not found (or in another workspace)
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : SprintScopeForm emits notFound; the dialog closes with Outdated; the opening page rereads\nand shows its own state
    else Sprint Closed (L2-023.4)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 closed, with recorded closing actor and instant; history unchanged
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (sprint closed)
      client --> page : closed: the alert region names who closed it and when and describes the dialog;\nView sprints only when offerSprintsLink is true; focus moves to the first action, View sprints or Close;\nno retry. SprintScopeForm emits outdated, so Close returns\nOutdated and the opening page rereads
    else Sprint still Planned
      handler --> ctrl : 409 not active; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not active)
      client --> page : closed presentation: Sprint 9 hasn't started, so its stories change in Plan stories; no retry;\nSprintScopeForm emits outdated, so Close returns Outdated and the opening page rereads
    else Done, foreign-workspace or already-member story to add; story to remove no longer a member (L2-022.2, L2-023.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 400 identifying each story; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails per story
      client --> page : allocated presentation: keep the selection; mark each story to add with its reason; focus moves to\nthe first marked story's checkbox (aria-disabled, so it stays focusable and reads its reason). Remove mode:\nthe story is dropped and named neutrally, "HCK-118 is no longer in Sprint 8"; Return to backlog becomes\nunavailable and focus moves to the alert (unconfirmed-added). No Retry or reference ID
    else Story to add is in another open sprint (L2-022.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 naming the story and its sprint; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (already allocated)
      client --> page : allocated state: keep the selection; mark the story and name its sprint; focus moves to\nits checkbox (aria-disabled); no Retry or reference ID
    else Stale sprint version
      handler --> ctrl : 409 changed since opened; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (stale version)
      client --> page : stale state: keep the selection; reload the sprint and the eligible list once and adopt\nthe new version; neutral "Sprint 8 changed after you opened this"; no resubmission; a chosen story\nnow in this sprint leaves the selection, named "HCK-130 is already in Sprint 8" (unconfirmed-added)
    else Change accepted
      handler -> entity : L2-023 changeScope(add, remove, at, actorId); initial scope unchanged
      entity --> handler : OpenSprintMembership children added or removed; SprintScopeChange children appended
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent; SaveChangesAsync: tracked sprint children and board placements;\nsprint version increments; success audit; one transaction
      alt Unique open-membership violation (concurrent allocation, L2-041.2)
        db --> handler : Roll back everything
        handler --> ctrl : 409 naming the story; nothing changed
        ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (already allocated)
        client --> page : allocated state: keep the selection; mark the story
      else Commit fails
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-save claim
        client --> page : Failed state with reference ID; selection kept;\nthe action retries only when chosen
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : New sprint version
        handler --> ctrl : Updated scope
        ctrl --> client : 200 with scope and version
        client --> page : SprintScopeForm emits changed(ScopeChangeSummary); the dialog closes with Changed; the opening\npage increments its counter (the board rereads its columns and scope log); a removed story returns\nto the backlog unchanged
        page --> actor : The opening page shows the "Scope updated" toast with the summary; focus returns to the trigger
      end
    end
  end
end
note over ctrl, db
A workspace lock wait beyond the timeout returns 503 with Retry-After and no change;
the dialog shows the same failed state with the reference ID.
An unexpected 403 (access changed after sign-in) changes nothing; SprintScopeForm keeps the selection and
emits forbidden, which the dialog relays as its own forbidden while it stays open, and the opening
page shows the "Your access changed" toast through TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry.
A change that gets no response is uncertain: the dialog keeps the selection, says "We couldn't
confirm whether Sprint 8's scope changed." (no reference ID), and the form emits unconfirmed,
which the dialog relays while it stays open, so the opening page rereads at once. The form
reloads the sprint and the eligible list once without the stale copy: a chosen story now in the
sprint is dropped and named "HCK-130 is already in Sprint 8", and in remove mode a story that
left is named "HCK-118 is no longer in Sprint 8" (unconfirmed-added), before Add or Return to
backlog is offered again for what remains. A sprint read Closed shows the neutral "Sprint 8 is
closed now." (never "nothing was changed") with View sprints when offered and Close, which
returns Outdated (unconfirmed-closed).
SaveChangesAsync raises ConcurrencyConflictException on a stale version, mapped to the same 409.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
